{"id":"mahabharata-1-180","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":180,"title":"अशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 180 · The kings attack Drupada","summary":{"en":"Enraged that Drupada would give his daughter to a Brahmin, the kings rise to kill him. Bhima uproots a tree and Arjuna takes up his bow to defend him, and Krishna, recognising them, tells Balarama that these are the Pandavas, alive.","kn":"ದ್ರುಪದನು ಮಗಳನ್ನು ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನಿಗೆ ಕೊಡುವನೆಂದು ಕೋಪಗೊಂಡ ರಾಜರು ಅವನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಲು ಏಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಭೀಮನು ಮರವನ್ನು ಕಿತ್ತು, ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಬಿಲ್ಲೆತ್ತಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ರಕ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅವರನ್ನು ಗುರುತಿಸಿದ ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಇವರು ಬದುಕಿರುವ ಪಾಂಡವರೆಂದು ಬಲರಾಮನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"द्रुपद द्वारा पुत्री को एक ब्राह्मण को देने से क्रुद्ध राजा उन्हें मारने उठते हैं। भीम एक वृक्ष उखाड़ लेते हैं और अर्जुन धनुष उठाकर उनकी रक्षा करते हैं, और उन्हें पहचानकर श्रीकृष्ण बलराम से कहते हैं कि ये जीवित पाण्डव हैं।","te":"ద్రుపదుడు కుమార్తెను బ్రాహ్మణునికి ఇస్తున్నాడని కోపించిన రాజులు అతనిని చంపడానికి లేస్తారు. భీముడు చెట్టును పెకలించి, అర్జునుడు విల్లు పట్టి అతనిని రక్షిస్తారు; వారిని గుర్తించిన శ్రీకృష్ణుడు వీరు జీవించి ఉన్న పాండవులని బలరామునికి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"த்ருபதன் மகளை ஓர் அந்தணனுக்குக் கொடுப்பதால் சினமுற்ற மன்னர்கள் அவனைக் கொல்ல எழுகிறார்கள். பீமன் ஒரு மரத்தைப் பிடுங்கியும் அர்ஜுனன் வில்லேந்தியும் அவனைக் காக்க, அவர்களை அடையாளம் கண்ட ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் இவர்கள் உயிருடன் இருக்கும் பாண்டவர்கள் என்று பலராமரிடம் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"തന്റെ മകളെ ഒരു ബ്രാഹ്മണന് നൽകുന്നതിൽ ദ്രുപദനോട് കോപിച്ച് രാജാക്കന്മാർ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വധിക്കാൻ എഴുന്നേൽക്കുന്നു. ഭീമൻ ഒരു മരം പിഴുതെടുക്കുന്നു, അദ്ദേഹത്തെ സംരക്ഷിക്കാൻ അർജുനൻ വില്ലെടുക്കുന്നു; അവരെ തിരിച്ചറിഞ്ഞ കൃഷ്ണൻ ഇവർ ജീവനോടെയുള്ള പാണ്ഡവരാണെന്ന് ബലരാമനോട് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.180; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"स्वयंवरपर्व","titleEn":"Svayamvara Parva (Draupadi's bridegroom choice)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मै दित्सति कन्यां तु ब्राह्मणाय महात्मने ।\nकोप आसीन्महीपानामालोक्यान्योन्यमन्तिकात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Drupada was ready to give his daughter to that great-souled Brahmin, anger arose among the kings as they looked at one another nearby."}},{"n":2,"text":"अस्मानयमतिक्रम्य तृणीकृत्य च संगतान् ।\nदातुमिच्छति विप्राय द्रौपदीं योषितां वराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They said: He has passed over us and treated us gathered here as straw, and wants to give Draupadi, best of women, to a Brahmin."}},{"n":3,"text":"निहन्मैनं दुरात्मानं योऽयमस्मान्न मन्यते ।\nन ह्यर्हत्येष सत्कारं नापि वृद्धक्रमं गुणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let us kill this wicked man who does not respect us; he does not deserve honour, nor the rank of age, by his qualities."}},{"n":4,"text":"हन्मैनं सह पुत्रेण दुराचारं नृपद्विषम् ।\nअयं हि सर्वानाहूय सत्कृत्य च नराधिपान् ।\nगुणवद्भोजयित्वा च ततः पश्चाद्विनिन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let us kill this ill-behaved enemy of kings along with his son. He called all the kings, honoured them, fed them well, and afterwards insults them."}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्मिन्राजसमावाये देवानामिव संनये ।\nकिमयं सदृशं कंचिन्नृपतिं नैव दृष्टवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this gathering of kings, like a meeting of the gods, did he not see a single king who was a fit match?"}},{"n":6,"text":"न च विप्रेष्वधीकारो विद्यते वरणं प्रति ।\nस्वयंवरः क्षत्रियाणामितीयं प्रथिता श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins have no right to the choosing; it is the well-known tradition that a svayamvara belongs to Kshatriyas."}},{"n":7,"text":"अथ वा यदि कन्येयं नेह कंचिद्बुभूषति ।\nअग्नावेनां परिक्षिप्य याम राष्ट्राणि पार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or if this girl wishes for none of us here, let us throw her into the fire and go back to our kingdoms, kings."}},{"n":8,"text":"ब्राह्मणो यदि वा बाल्याल्लोभाद्वा कृतवानिदम् ।\nविप्रियं पार्थिवेन्द्राणां नैष वध्यः कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"If a Brahmin did this out of youthful thoughtlessness or greed, which displeases the lords of kings, he must in no way be killed."}},{"n":9,"text":"ब्राह्मणार्थं हि नो राज्यं जीवितं च वसूनि च ।\nपुत्रपौत्रं च यच्चान्यदस्माकं विद्यते धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For our kingdom, our lives, our wealth, our sons and grandsons and whatever other riches we have are for the sake of Brahmins."}},{"n":10,"text":"अवमानभयादेतत्स्वधर्मस्य च रक्षणात् ।\nस्वयंवराणां चान्येषां मा भूदेवंविधा गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is to guard against insult and to protect our own duty, so that no such fate befalls other svayamvaras."}},{"n":11,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा राजशार्दूला हृष्टाः परिघबाहवः ।\nद्रुपदं संजिघृक्षन्तः सायुधाः समुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, those tigers among kings, delighted, with arms like iron bars, rushed at Drupada with weapons, wishing to seize him."}},{"n":12,"text":"तान्गृहीतशरावापान्क्रुद्धानापततो नृपान् ।\nद्रुपदो वीक्ष्य संत्रासाद्ब्राह्मणाञ्शरणं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the angry kings rushing upon him with bows and arrows in hand, Drupada in terror took refuge with the Brahmins."}},{"n":13,"text":"वेगेनापततस्तांस्तु प्रभिन्नानिव वारणान् ।\nपाण्डुपुत्रौ महावीर्यौ प्रतीयतुररिंदमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two sons of Pandu, of great valour and subduers of enemies, went to meet those kings rushing like rutting elephants."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततः समुत्पेतुरुदायुधास्ते\nमहीक्षितो बद्धतलाङ्गुलित्राः ।\nजिघांसमानाः कुरुराजपुत्रा-\nवमर्षयन्तोऽर्जुनभीमसेनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those kings with raised weapons and fingers guarded with gloves sprang up, wishing to kill the two Kuru princes, Arjuna and Bhimasena, who could not bear it."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततस्तु भीमोऽद्भुतवीर्यकर्मा\nमहाबलो वज्रसमानवीर्यः ।\nउत्पाट्य दोर्भ्यां द्रुममेकवीरो\nनिष्पत्रयामास यथा गजेन्द्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, of marvellous valour and deeds, mighty and with strength like the thunderbolt, uprooted a tree with his arms and stripped it of leaves like a lord of elephants."}},{"n":16,"text":"तं वृक्षमादाय रिपुप्रमाथी\nदण्डीव दण्डं पितृराज उग्रम् ।\nतस्थौ समीपे पुरुषर्षभस्य\nपार्थस्य पार्थः पृथुदीर्घबाहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking that tree, the crusher of foes, long-armed Bhima, stood near Partha, bull among men, like the king of the dead with his dread staff."}},{"n":17,"text":"तत्प्रेक्ष्य कर्मातिमनुष्यबुद्धे-\nर्जिष्णोः सहभ्रातुरचिन्त्यकर्मा ।\nदामोदरो भ्रातरमुग्रवीर्यं\nहलायुधं वाक्यमिदं बभाषे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that deed of Arjuna and his brother, beyond human understanding, Damodara of unthinkable deeds spoke to his fierce and valiant brother, Balarama the plough-bearer."}},{"n":18,"text":"य एष मत्तर्षभतुल्यगामी\nमहद्धनुः कर्षति तालमात्रम् ।\nएषोऽर्जुनो नात्र विचार्यमस्ति\nयद्यस्मि संकर्षण वासुदेवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: If I am Vasudeva, Sankarshana, then there is no doubt: this one who walks like a rutting bull and draws a great bow the length of a palm tree is Arjuna."}},{"n":19,"text":"य एष वृक्षं तरसावरुज्य\nराज्ञां विकारे सहसा निवृत्तः ।\nवृकोदरो नान्य इहैतदद्य\nकर्तुं समर्थो भुवि मर्त्यधर्मा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one who tore up a tree by force and quickly turned back, at the kings' attack, is Vrikodara and no one else; no mortal on earth could do this today."}},{"n":20,"text":"योऽसौ पुरस्तात्कमलायताक्ष-\nस्तनुर्महासिंहगतिर्विनीतः ।\nगौरः प्रलम्बोज्ज्वलचारुघोणो\nविनिःसृतः सोऽच्युत धर्मराजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Achyuta, the one earlier, lotus-eyed, slender, with the gait of a great lion, modest, fair, with a long, bright, handsome nose, who went out, is Dharmaraja."}},{"n":21,"text":"यौ तौ कुमाराविव कार्त्तिकेयौ\nद्वावश्विनेयाविति मे प्रतर्कः ।\nमुक्ता हि तस्माज्जतुवेश्मदाहा-\nन्मया श्रुताः पाण्डुसुताः पृथा च ॥","meaning":{"en":"And those two youths like the Kartikeyas, I guess, are the twin sons of the Ashvins. I have heard that the sons of Pandu and Pritha were freed from the burning of the house of lac."}},{"n":22,"text":"तमब्रवीन्निर्मलतोयदाभो\nहलायुधोऽनन्तरजं प्रतीतः ।\nप्रीतोऽस्मि दिष्ट्या हि पितृष्वसा नः\nपृथा विमुक्ता सह कौरवाग्र्यैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Balarama, dark like a clear cloud, answered his younger brother with confidence: I am glad that our father's sister Pritha has been freed along with the foremost Kauravas."}}]}]}